\begin{lemma}[Martingale central limit theorem]
Let $\{\xi_{Tt}\in\mathbb R,\mathcal F_{Tt}: 1\le t\le T, T\ge 1\}$ be an array of square-integrable martingale difference sequences. Let $\mathcal V_T=\sum_{t=1}^T\mathbb E(\xi^2_{Tt}\mid\mathcal F_{T,t-1})$, where $\mathcal F_{T0}$ is trivial, and $V_T=\mathbb E(\mathcal V_T)$. As $T\to\infty$, if (i) $\mathcal V_T/V_T=1+o_P(1)$; (ii) $V_T^{-1}\sum_{t=1}^T\mathbb E\{\xi_{Tt}^2\mathbf1(|\xi_{Tt}|\geq\epsilon V_T^{-1/2})\}=o_P(1)$ for all $\epsilon>0$, then $V_T^{-1/2}\sum_{t=1}^T\xi_{Tt}\Rightarrow\mathcal N(0,1)$.
\end{lemma}
